  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8eadae48e7a34ac3bc00654cd6a3d6d6",
      "statement": "src/mimetype.rs is the single owner of the project's format vocabulary: lowercase dotless extension constants, a lazily built infer::Infer matcher, and the ARCHIVE_EXTENSIONS / PS3_EXTENSIONS / NON_ORIGINAL_EXTENSIONS groups. It exposes one detection entry point, `pub async fn get_mimetype(path) -> Result<Option<Type>>`, which borrows the shared static MATCHER so one table serves all callers and maps I/O failure to \"Failed to infer MIME type\"; Ok(None) is a normal \"no matcher fired\" answer, not an error.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/mimetype.rs#L100-L122",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0381e0d753e42fe41f43bc7a1e0cd9c88e4e2ba62d9105b2ed99361d36bf0590:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/mimetype.rs#L6-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6340dbf6fcdb51d0dcaad0bdc6cf13b90a09db34ee0d21a1f01a9446e3f51e0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d5831a846594c458604cc998d79bbf7",
      "statement": "init_matcher() starts from Infer::new() (keeping the crate's built-in zip/7z/gzip detection) and registers ten ROM-specific magic-byte matchers — BPS \"BPS1\", CHD \"MComprHD\" (8 bytes), CSO \"CISO\", IPS \"PATCH\" (5 bytes), IRD \"3IRD\", RDSK \"RDSK\", RIFF \"RIFF\", RVZ \"RVZ\"+0x01, XDELTA D6 C3 C4 (3 bytes) and ZSO with the magic \"ZISO\" — each as a pure &[u8] -> bool that checks buf.len() before indexing so truncated headers return false instead of panicking. RVZ pins the version byte to 0x01, so a future RVZ revision is not detected by content.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/mimetype.rs#L47-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4c2e40f7e5acb9797abe964b130b7e7b4be2ee901698cbe39a7261cbf9f56f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff5c3fdd575244c2ae59101279246085",
      "statement": "Because each matcher is registered with an extension constant, `Type::extension()` returns exactly that constant, which is why callers across the codebase compare mimetype.extension() against CHD_EXTENSION, ARCHIVE_EXTENSIONS and PatchType/XsoType strum variants; roughly twenty modules import the whole module with `use super::mimetype::*;`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/import_patches.rs#L94-L100",
