    {
      "id": "claim_e56a662f3cf142baa8f5de2c1c4aec3e",
      "statement": "Format-entry guards validate inconsistently, and the difference is externally visible: as_chd, as_riff, as_rdsk and as_xso call get_mimetype and bail when nothing matches (as_xso deriving XsoType from the mimetype extension, so cso and zso share one romfile type), while as_rvz, as_nsz, as_nsp and AsArchive::as_archive only compare path.extension() lowercased against their constant (or ArchiveType::from_str). RVZ consequently has a magic matcher its own guard never consults — it exists for batch partitioning and content-first callers — and NSZ/NSP are typed by name alone.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/archive.rs#L385-L416",
