    {
      "id": "claim_c70a6486e1f148c2a551488973f3285f",
      "statement": "Patches rely on content with no filename fallback: parse_patch maps PatchType::from_str(mimetype.extension()) and a file no matcher recognizes is reported as \"Unsupported patch format\". parse_ird likewise requires a mimetype and uses it to choose the reader — gz triggers a GzDecoder wrapper, ird reads raw, anything else bails \"Not an IRD file\" — which only works because infer's built-in gzip matcher shares the same MATCHER table.",
      "evidence": [
